---
/**
 * Refund policy for HD credit packs. Paddle (the Merchant of Record) requires a
 * window of 14 to 90 days and refunds through paddle.net; never "no refunds".
 * The ledger takes refunded credits back (server/api.ts, supabase/migrations).
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import { CONTACT, REFUND_DAYS, SELLER, UPDATED } from '../data/legal'
---

<Page title="Refund policy · Inlay" description={`A full refund on any Inlay credit pack within ${REFUND_DAYS} days.`}>
  <article class="prose" aria-labelledby="refunds-title">
    <h1 id="refunds-title">Refund policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">If HD mode isn't right for you, you can have your money back within {REFUND_DAYS} days of buying.</p>

    <h2>What you can get back</h2>
    <p>
      A full refund of any credit pack, for any reason, if you ask within {REFUND_DAYS} days of buying it. The pack's credits are taken off
      your account when you ask; if Paddle declines the refund, they come back.
    </p>
    <p>
      An HD run that fails gives its credits back automatically, so you never pay for a result you didn't get. If a result is poor rather than
      missing, tell us: we'll look at it and return the credits where it's fair.
    </p>

    <h2>How to ask</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases are made through Paddle, our reseller and the Merchant of Record, so refunds go through Paddle too. Find your order at <a
        href="https://paddle.net">paddle.net</a> using the email address on your receipt, or reply to the receipt email. You can also email
      us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> and we'll arrange it.
    </p>
    <p>Refunds go back to the card or account you paid with. Paddle usually processes them within a few days; your bank may take longer to show them.</p>

    <h2>After {REFUND_DAYS} days</h2>
    <p>
      Credits never expire, so there's no deadline to use them. After {REFUND_DAYS} days we can still refund where the law requires it, or
      where something on our side went wrong.
    </p>

    <p class="fine">Inlay is operated by {SELLER}. Last updated {UPDATED}.</p>
  </article>
</Page>
